    "description": "Deterministic subject-held-out ensemble. It builds three independent trial-level feature views: raw optical-density dynamics with fixed temporal projections, within-trial spatially centered dynamics, and homologous left/right-hemisphere contrasts based on the symmetric channel ordering. Each candidate uses train-fold robust scaling, clipping, univariate feature selection, and a class-balanced linear classifier. Hyperparameters are selected by mean balanced accuracy across seven leave-one-subject-out folds, using the seven contiguous 54-trial subject blocks implied by the supplied training design. The best candidate from each sufficiently predictive feature view is refit on all training trials, and standardized decision scores are combined with validation-derived reliability weights. No test-set fitting or cross-trial aggregation is used.",
